title: Route1Thu1Start
tags: cutscene
---
<<declare $r1_dishes_started = false>>
<<declare $r1_dishes_turn = "">>
<<declare $r1_dinner_shelf = false>>
// The entry node of box R1Dinner1, started by going to bed on Sunday (bed_3b.yarn).
// Thursday evening on the landing. What the box owns is reset here: the dishes, the
// shelf's word, and where the socks are (nobody remembers Sunday).
<<enter_box R1Dinner1>>
<<set $r1_dishes_started to false>>
<<set $r1_dishes_turn to "">>
<<set $r1_dinner_shelf to false>>
<<set $r1_socks_at to "">>
<<fade_out>>
<<place Player PlayerArrive>>
<<face Player right>>
<<card "Thursday. Eight o'clock.">>
<<fade_in>>
<<phone PhoneThursday1>>
<<note r1_thu1 "A text from Samantha.">>
You: Thursday. And my phone's buzzing.
===
title: Route1Thu1Door
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by knocking on 3A on the first Thursday (door_3a.yarn).
<<walk Player PlayerTo3A>>
<<face Player right>>
<<wait 1>>
<<open_door Door3A>>
<<show Samantha>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaOut>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Eight o'clock. You're learning.
{$samantha_name}: Empty-handed. Good. You listened.
{$samantha_name}: Come in. You know the rule.
You: Shoes off.
{$samantha_name}: Good.
// She goes back to her stove; he follows her in.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToKitchen3A no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerInto3A>>
<<await_walks>>
<<close_door Door3A>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Five minutes. Look around if you want.
{$samantha_name}: Don't touch the knives. Sit down when you're ready.
<<done R1Dinner1 door>>
<<note r1_thu1 "Dinner at hers. Sit at her table.">>
// The player now walks around her flat. Sitting at the table starts Route1Dinner (table_3a.yarn).
===
title: Route1Dinner
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by sitting down at her table on the first Thursday (table_3a.yarn).
<<place Player PlayerSit>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaSit>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Pasta. Don't look so surprised.
You: It smells great.
{$samantha_name}: I know.
{$samantha_name}: I study people, you know. It's practically my job.
<<if is_done("R1Dinner1", "peek")>>
    // PLACEHOLDER lines: he looked at her notebook before she showed it.
    {$samantha_name}: And you already had your hand on my notebook. So you know there's a page about you.
    You: I didn't read it.
    {$samantha_name}: Then I'll read it to you.
<<else>>
    {$samantha_name}: After the viewing I wrote down a few lines about you. I do it with everyone who sees the flat.
    {$samantha_name}: I'll read them to you.
<<endif>>
{$samantha_name}: "Keen to please. Waits to be told. Doesn't know it yet."
// PLACEHOLDER: replaces the reply menu.
You: ...Maybe.
{$samantha_name}: Maybe. That's the most honest thing you've said all week.
{$samantha_name}: Anyway. I cooked, so you wash up.
You: Is that a rule too?
{$samantha_name}: It is now. The sink's over there. Take your time. I like to watch.
<<done R1Dinner1 dinner>>
<<note r1_thu1 "Wash up. Her sink.">>
// The player walks to the sink himself. Using it starts Route1Dishes (sink_3a.yarn).
===
title: Route1Dishes
tags: cutscene
---
// Started at her sink after dinner (sink_3a.yarn). It stops on her order; the sink then
// offers "Keep washing" and "Turn around", and either goes on with Route1DishesEnd.
<<walk Player PlayerAtSink>>
<<face Player up>>
<<wait 2>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaBehindSink>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
{$samantha_name}: You missed a spot.
You: Where?
{$samantha_name}: Don't turn around. Keep washing.
<<set $r1_dishes_started to true>>
<<note r1_thu1 "Keep washing.">>
===
title: Route1DishesEnd
tags: cutscene
---
// Started from her sink once he keeps washing or has turned around (sink_3a.yarn).
<<if $r1_dishes_turn == "stay">>
    {$samantha_name}: See? Easy.
<<endif>>
<<wait 2>>
{$samantha_name}: You did well tonight.
// She kisses his cheek from behind.
{$samantha_name}: That's for doing as you're told.
{$samantha_name}: Next Thursday. Same time. I'll text you what to bring.
You: And if I'm busy?
{$samantha_name}: You won't be.
// She sees him out.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToDoor3AInside>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<open_door Door3A>>
<<walk Player PlayerOutOf3A>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Goodnight, neighbour.
<<close_door Door3A>>
<<done R1Dinner1 dishes>>
<<note r1_thu1 "Home. Bed.">>
===
title: PhoneThursday1
tags: phone
---
// Her text on the first Thursday, delivered by Route1Thu1Start. The wine she names is the
// clue for the second Thursday. PLACEHOLDER lines.
{$samantha_name}: Eight. Mine. Not five to.
{$samantha_name}: Don't bring anything. I drink Red Fox, the 2021, and I have it.
{$samantha_name}: Not the one with the gold label. Remember that.
-> Got it.
    {$samantha_name}: Good.
-> What's wrong with the gold label?
    {$samantha_name}: It tries too hard.
<<done R1Dinner1 text>>
<<done R1Dinner1 wine>>
<<note r1_thu1 "Dinner at hers. 3A, eight. Bring nothing.">>
<<note r1_wine "She drinks Red Fox. The 2021, not the gold label.">>
===
